--[[
NOTES
- v9.1 register fix: Luau allows 200 local variables per function and a script's top level counts as
  one function. Sections are wrapped in do ... end so their helpers stop counting. When you add new
  features, wrap them in do ... end too (only keep a local at the top level if another section needs it,
  and use "local name" before the block + "function name()" inside it).

- Fire Method:
    LMB Spam       one clean click per shot (release -> press -> release), every Fire Delay but never
                   faster than ~20/s, for as long as the bot stays locked on. Needs VirtualInputManager
                   or mouse1press, otherwise only the BotFire attribute is set
    LMB Hold       holds left mouse while on target, releases when the target is lost
    Tool Activate  only tool:Activate() (left-click style)
    Both           LMB spam + tool:Activate()
  The click happens at your mouse position, so keep the GUI out from under the cursor
  (minimize it with the Minimize Key) or the click lands on the GUI instead of the game.

- Reading the status line while sniping: "sniping X | LMB spam (...) shot #N".
    * N keeps going up but the gun doesn't fire  -> the game is ignoring the clicks (cooldown, or the
      cursor is over the GUI). Try hooking BotFire (below).
    * N stops going up while still locked        -> tell me, that would be a bug in the bot.

- DeathFix (Bot tab + Aimbot tab toggles): EVERYONE who dies is handled, not just your kills.
  Deaths come from the Killed remote (any killer/victim), Humanoid.Died, and a player's old Character
  being replaced on respawn. The dead character is marked (bot/aimbot ignore it at once), that player's
  ESP is deleted (nobody else's), and body models that show up with their name, or around the time and
  place of the death, are marked too. A respawned player is a new model, so they work normally again.
  A non-player lock whose health doesn't change for 4s is dropped as a stuck body.
  If the remote can't be found you get a warning in the output.

- Auto Spawn: does NOT spam. When the Killed remote says YOU died it waits "Delay After Death"
  (0.5s) and presses the spawn key (Space). "Retry Until Respawned" presses again every
  "Retry Interval" (max 6 times) until you get a new character.

- NPC targeting / dead bodies: with "NPC Hitbox Part (required)" = Hitbox, an NPC is only a target
  while it has a part with that name, and the instant that part is removed it is dropped (checked every
  frame). Blank the field to target any NPC model.

- Works in any game, but for YOUR game the most reliable hook is in your weapon's LocalScript:
      tool:GetAttributeChangedSignal("BotFire"):Connect(shoot)
  The bot sets the "BotFire" attribute on the tool every time it fires (and on your player).

- Presets: Save writes everything (all settings, colors, rainbow flags, keybinds, script slots).
  The preset you saved last loads automatically on start. bot.enabled is deliberately NOT stored,
  so the bot never starts by itself.
]]
